{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit `theta ~ uniform(0, 1)` prior before the likelihood. This is density-neutral for `theta`, which is already constrained to `[0, 1]`, and satisfies SafeStan's requirement that each parameter have exactly one built-in prior before use. The likelihood remains `y ~ bernoulli(theta[z])`; `z`, `K`, and `N` are context data, not protected observations. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"/**
 * Straightforward Bernoulli formulation.
 */
data {
  int<lower=1> K; // num arms
  int<lower=0> N; // num trials
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> z; // arm on trial n
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y; // reward on trial n
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] theta; // arm return prob
}
model {
  theta ~ uniform(0, 1);
  y ~ bernoulli(theta[z]); // i.i.d. by arm
}
generated quantities {
  simplex[K] is_best; // one hot or uniform with ties
  {
    real best_prob = max(theta);
    for (k in 1 : K) {
      is_best[k] = theta[k] >= best_prob;
    }
    is_best /= sum(is_best); // uniform for ties
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":4,"N":1,"y":[0],"z":[3]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
